"recipients" refer to individuals or organizations that receive the
Program.

  "Modify" means to copy from or adapt all or part of the work in a
fashion requiring copyright permission, other than the making of an
exact copy.  The resulting work is called a "modified version" of the
earlier work or a work "derived from" the earlier work.

  A "covered work" means either the unmodified Program or a work based
on the Program.

  "Propagate" a work means to do anything with it that, without
permission, would make you directly or indirectly liable for
infringement under applicable copyright law, except executing it on
your own premises or with equipment you own or control.  Propagation
includes copying, distribution (with or without modification), making
available to the public, and in some contexts, making it available to
third parties.  The activities of a person running a program on their
own premises or with equipment they own or control are not considered
propagation if the result is not made available to third parties.

  "Convey" a work means to propagate it so that another party can make
or receive copies.  Mere interaction with a user through a computer
network, with no transfer of a copy, is not conveying.

  An interactive user interface displays "Appropriate Legal Notices"
to the extent that it includes a convenient and prominently visible
feature that (1) displays an appropriate copyright notice, and (2)
tells the user that there is no warranty for the work (except to the
extent that warranties are provided), and (3) conveys the substance
of this License to the user.  For complex works, the portion of the
user interface that provides the feature described above may not
cover the entire interface.

